Valid UTF-8 is UTF-8, and two traces on the data to string path

ICU ucsdet answers ISO-8859-1 for plain ASCII, so a five byte text file detected as Latin-1 here
where a Mac answers UTF-8. The detector now prefers UTF-8 whenever the whole buffer validates as
it, with a NUL guard so BOM-less UTF-16, whose zero bytes are individually valid UTF-8, still falls
through to ICU. Measured: the same five bytes now detect as encoding 4 where they detected as 5.

Two traces under CIDER_TRACE_TEXT paid for themselves finding this and stay. CIDER_STRDETECT prints
what the detector chose and the converted string length, low volume since it only fires on a file
read. CIDER_STRBYTES prints ONLY a nil conversion, since every ObjC data to string call funnels
through initWithBytes and printing success would drown the log.

For the record of task #194: this was suspect one and it is now dead in both forms. The conversion
was never failing, and with the encoding corrected to match macOS the iA Writer editor storage
still measures len=0, so the starvation lies in the application hand-off, not in data to string.
